.TH NYBBLE 1 "July 2026" "nybble 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nybble \- programmer's calculator for hardware engineers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nybble
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Nybble
is a native desktop calculator for FPGA and hardware engineers. It shows one
value in hexadecimal, decimal, binary and octal simultaneously, supports
configurable bit widths (1\-128) and signedness, lets you toggle individual
bits, and evaluates bitwise and arithmetic expressions.
.PP
Expressions support the usual arithmetic and bitwise operators, the
.B **
power operator, and named functions
.RB ( sqrt ", " log2 ", " clog2 ", " gcd
and others in integer mode; the full scientific set plus
.BR pi ", " e " and " tau
in float mode). The identifier
.B ans
refers to the current value.
.PP
Nybble takes no command line arguments; all interaction is through the GUI.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PC_SIZE=\fIWIDTH\fRx\fIHEIGHT\fR
Override the initial window size. Useful for reproducing layout issues.
.TP
.B PC_DEBUG=1
Dump layout decisions and bit\-grid geometry to standard error.
.TP
.B PC_UPDATE_CHANNEL=beta
Also consider pre\-release builds when checking for updates. Unset (or any other
value) means stable releases only. Pre\-releases are release candidates and may
be unstable; there is no automatic way back to the stable channel short of
reinstalling.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nybble/app.ron
Settings and calculation history. Shared with the portable and AppImage builds,
and deliberately preserved when the package is removed.
.SH NOTES
This build uses the X11 backend, so on Wayland desktops it runs through
XWayland.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/fanaloka47/nybble/issues
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage: https://github.com/fanaloka47/nybble
